{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC3 audit — remaining --json mutation wrappers in acli_cli_ops (and the module-level acli.py wrappers), checked for the raw-passthrough pattern this ticket fixed in add_comment:\n\n- create_issue paths (_create_issue_no_json, _create_from_json_payload): both return the CompletedProcess to _create_issue_from_json, which routes stdout through _verify_created_issue (parses, REST/subprocess-verifies, raises loudly on missing key). NOT raw passthrough. OK.\n- update_priority: REST PUT via urllib, returns None, no ACLI JSON parse. OK.\n- get_issue: unwraps issues[0], raises 'Issue not found' when absent. OK (read).\n- get_comments -> _parse_paginated_comments -> _parse_acli_comments: normalizes bare-list/wrapped-dict/unrecognized shapes. OK (read).\n- add_comment: fixed by this ticket (_parse_comment_created; Gerrit change 2144).\n\nFINDING (latent, same class): module-level acli.update_issue (acli.py, 'workitem edit --json' branch) still returns raw json.loads(result.stdout) — the batch mutation envelope — while its docstring/type suggest an issue resource. Mitigations today: _run_acli's _check_mutation_failure raises AcliMutationError on FAILURE envelopes (bug 44de), and the only production consumer chain (dispatch_one._update_one_scalar_update -> update_one -> apply_handlers.handle_update) treats the return opaquely (None-or-dict; no field reads), so no consumer-reachable hazard exists today. Not fixed here to keep this change surgical; flagging for a follow-up if a consumer ever starts reading fields from update_issue's return."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787454654776152001,"uuid":"1809e5f2-46aa-4142-a2ba-f59f931c7019"}